\b Pros:\b0\par
    Less limited_With Varsity Tutors you can upload as many texts as you want for free. A possible downside is that each text must be under 10000 characters just like LessonUp.
    Extra_This AI-tool has many different features that can help you save time.  Lesson plan generator  and  rubric generator  are two of the other AI features that Varsity Tutors offers. Most of these features are free of use.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Slow_Varsity Tutors takes longer to adapt a text compared to similar AI-tools like Kira or SchoolAI.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.1.8 Flint\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://flintk12.com/tools/ai-text-leveler
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Flint&from=subcat&subcategory=Adapting%20texts&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Flint\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Multilingual_Flint supports a wide range of languages.
    Extra_There are multiple features you can access with Flint apart from the text adapter. All of these features are free to use. Most of these features are similar to SchoolAI or CoGrader for example. Next to a lesson plan generator and a rubric generator Flint also has a worksheet generator and a feature for grading papers.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Complex_Finding all the features on Flint is not easy. To see them you need to ask Sparky (your AI teaching assistant). Once you click on it the AI features appear and you can select the one you want to use.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.1.9 CoGrader\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://cograder.com/reading-level-conversion/
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=CoGrader&from=subcat&subcategory=Adapting%20texts&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul CoGrader\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Less limited_ CoGrader is a completely free AI-tool you can use to adapt text to different reading levels. There is no limit to the number of characters you can use compared to Varity Tutors or LessonUp.
    Extra_Just like similar AI-tools such as Knowt or Flint this AI tool has a few other features you can use. One of these is the  originality checker . This feature allows you to see whether a text is written by AI or not. It also includes an AI rubric generator among many other features.
    Advanced_CoGrader allows you to upload handwritten essays and grade them.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Quality_Compared to Diffit this AI feature for adapting text is a bit weaker because CoGrader is originally an AI grading tool.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.1.10 Knowt\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://knowt.com/home
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Knowt&from=subcat&subcategory=Adapting%20texts&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Knowt\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Extra_Just like similar AI-tools Knowt has multiple features apart from the text adapter to help teachers. For example it includes a lesson plan generator and a PowerPoint summarizer.
    Multilingual_Knowt has a wide range of languages that it supports.
    Editing_After adapting your text to a certain grade level you can edit it manually. Knowt has a built-in text editor where you can change almost anything and even add images.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Login required_To use Knowt you need to create an account. This AI-tool will ask you who you are and if you select teacher you will have less access to certain features than if you select the student option.
    Slow_Compared to CoGrader or LessonUp this AI tool is slower.
    Complex_Knowt can feel a bit difficult at first when trying to access all the AI features. They are not visible on the homepage so to find them you need to use the search bar.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.1.11 Teacher Quill\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://teachquill.com/ai-text-leveler
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Teacher%20Quill&from=subcat&subcategory=Adapting%20texts&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Teacher Quill\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Options_Apart from asking which grade level the text is meant for the AI tool also asks certain pre-prompt questions to make it easier to adapt the text to your preferences.
    Extra_Similarly to Kira and Flint this AI-tool offers a bunch of other AI features especially ones for creating exercises just like Twee for example.
    More_Next to just rewriting your text Teacher Quill also adds a list of all the key changes it made to the text as well as some teaching tips.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Slow_Just like Knowt this AI-tool is a bit on the slower side.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.1.12 Blueye\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://blueye.org/tools/reading-level-converter
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Blueye&from=subcat&subcategory=Adapting%20texts&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Blueye\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Multilingual_Blueye supports a wide range of languages.
    Quality_The adapted text is overall okay but AI-tools such as Diffit or Flint are remarkably better.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Limited_With Blueye you are not able upload documents. To adapt a text you need to paste the text into the provided box.
    Slow_The more text you ask this AI-tool to adapt the longer it will take.
\par
\pard\b\fs28 3.2 Generating exercises\b0\fs24\line
\pard\i 3.2.1 Diffit - See 3.1.3 Diffit in Category Differentiation, Subcategory Adapting texts. \i0\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.2 Twee\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://www.twee.com
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Twee&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Twee\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\pard\ql\i Description: AI lesson planning and educational content generator.\i0\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Resource_Twee can provide you with a list of grammar rules for specific topics you ask for. It will also help you create exercises with answers based on the topic.
    Multilingual_Twee mostly focuses on English but it offers a variety of languages to create exercises. Specifically for English it also makes a clear distinction between British and American English.
    Fast_ Twee can create exercises very quickly. For example when you create a matching exercise with pictures and words it generates the activity and then suggests other related exercises you can create using the same content.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Limited usage_While there is still a lot you can do most features or lesson plans on Twee require the Pro version which you need to pay $10 a month for.
    Less-suitable_Most of the free ready-made lesson plans on Twee are very specific and are not always suitable for teachers who teach secondary school students between the ages of 12 and 16. This means that with the free version teachers may still need to adapt the material and lesson plan for their own class.
    Unverified_The grammar explanations and exercises are AI-generated which means they are not always fully accurate.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.3 TeachTools\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://teachtools.co/tools/worksheet-generator?welcome=1
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=TeachTools&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul TeachTools\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Fast_Generating a worksheet with TeachTools takes less than a minute.
    Extra_Just like Worksheetzone this AI-tool gives you access to a bunch of other features such as a lesson plan generator and a video summarizer.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Multilingual_Teachtools supports a few languages but only the ten most popular ones.
    Limited usage_With the free plan of TeachTools you can only generate up to three items a month. You can however use every feature that TeachTools offers. None of the extra features are locked behind a paywall.
    Correction key_ The answers to the exercises aren t included when generating a worksheet with TeachTools.
    Options_Although the AI-tool asks you how many different questions it should generate and for which grade level it doesn t specify what type of questions it will generate. This leads to there being a lot of small text with multiple-choice questions. You also cannot generate more than 20 questions in one setting.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.4 LessonOrca\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://lessonorca.com/
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=LessonOrca&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul LessonOrca\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Less limited_If you don t sign up you can only make three generations with the free plan. If you do sign up you will get unlimited access for at least two weeks.
    Correction key_Only when you sign in to LessonOrca you get the answers to your worksheet.
    Options_Before generating a worksheet LessonOrca asks a lot of pre-prompt questions to make the worksheet as close as possible to your idea.
    Extra_Next to the worksheet generator LessonOrca also provides a lesson plan generator that you can use for free.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Slow_LessonOrca can take a few minutes to create a worksheet.
    Quality_Just like TeachTools most of the generated questions are multiple-choice questions.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.5 Worksheet Wizard\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://worksheet-wizard.com/
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Worksheet%20Wizard&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Worksheet Wizard\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Fast_Worksheet Wizard generates exercises faster unlike other AI-tools such as LessonOrca or WorksheetZone for example.
    Multilingual_ Worksheet Wizard supports a variety of languages.
    Options_With Worksheet Wizard you can choose what type of exercises you want to generate unlike LessonOrca or TeachTools for example.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Limited usage_You can only generate five worksheets per month with the free version of Worksheet Wizard.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.6 Quizgecko\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://quizgecko.com/home
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=Quizgecko&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul Quizgecko\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Options_Similar to Worksheet Wizard you can choose what type of exercises you want to generate.
    Multilingual_Quizgecko offers a wide range of different languages.
    Correction key_Quizgecko provides the answers to your worksheet.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Limited usage_You can only generate a certain number of worksheets per month. Unlike other AI-tools though Quizgecko can generate up to 60 questions with a single prompt.
    Online_There is no option to download the exercises as a document. The questions are originally created as online exercises but you can copy and paste them into your own work document.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.7 WorksheetZone\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://worksheetzone.org/
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=WorksheetZone&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul WorksheetZone\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Correction key_With WorksheetZone you immediately get the answers to your worksheet.
    Multilingual_WorksheetZone supports a variety of languages.
    Options_With WorksheetZone you can choose the preferred grade and the duration of the exercises. You can also decide what kind of questions you want generated such as individual exercises or guided practice.
    Extra_WorksheetZone offers a bunch of other AI features. You can generate different exercises separately for specific types of questions. For example you may only want a crossword puzzle or a fill-in-the-blanks exercise. Not only that but WorksheetZone also offers a lesson plan generator as well as a rubric generator.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Slow_WorksheetZone takes a couple of minutes to generate a worksheet.
    Limited usage_You can only generate a few worksheets every month when using the free version.
\par
\pard\b\fs24 3.2.8 StudyGlenAI\b0\fs24\line
Website: https://studyglen.com/quiz
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thomasmorer0982323-cmyk.github.io/AI-Tools/AIEngine.html?engine=StudyGlenAI&from=subcat&subcategory=Generating%20exercises&category=Differentiation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf1\ul StudyGlenAI\ulnone\cf0}}}\par
\b Pros:\b0\par
    Options_Similar to Worksheet Wizard you can choose the type of questions StudyGlenAI generates for you. You have multiple options such as true-false or short-answer questions. This AI-tool can also create images that match the questions.
    Multilingual_StudyGlenAI supports over 37 languages.
    Correction key_StudyGlenAI provides the answers with every generated worksheet.
\b Cons:\b0\par
    Limited usage_The free version of StudyGlenAI includes only five generated questions.
    Slow_Compared to other AI tools StudyGlenAI can take up to 5 minutes to generate questions.
\par
